  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1155 AM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nThe center of the anomalous ridge will start to shift a little to\nour west on Friday as it interacts with an upper-low moving west \ntoward Florida. By then better tropospheric moisture is expected \nto wrap around into the eastern periphery of the ridge, basically \ndown through the Appalachians. This will support isolated diurnal \nconvection Friday into the weekend, mainly focused near and across\nthe Cumberland Plateau. \n\nForecast details for next week are a little less certain in some\nways, but medium-range guidance/ensembles suggest a decrease in \ntemperatures and increase in rain/storm chances as we are more \ninfluenced by systems passing to our north with a weaker ridge\nacross the Southeast. Associated presence of a front/surface\ntrough will also play a role in encouraging better convective\ncoverage early to mid week. Either way, the trend is an\nimprovement as conditions don't look as hot, but remain above-\nnormal temperature wise.",
